.\" karvi-config(1): the manual page of karvi's config word. Written by hand except
.\" the regions between the markers, which tools/mangen rewrites from the
.\" word's help text (make generate).
.TH KARVI-CONFIG 1 "" "karvi"
.\" Paths and options are not hyphenated, and lines are not stretched.
.nh
.ds AD l
.ad l
.SH NAME
karvi\-config \- configuration tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED SYNOPSIS: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
\fBkarvi\fR \fBconfig generate\fR [\-\-minimal|\-\-full] [\-\-force] [file]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBconfig validate\fR [\-\-format text|json] [file|dir]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBconfig show\fR [\-\-format toml|json] [\-\-explain] [\-\-show\-sources] [key...]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBconfig colors\fR
.\" END GENERATED SYNOPSIS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" BEGIN GENERATED DESCRIPTION: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
.PP
Options may appear before or after the positional argument; \-\- makes a later
argument beginning with a dash positional. \-\-help shows this text. config
colors prints every display.colors role in its colour, the configured theme
first and then the other: the key, the colour, what set it, and the escape.
Specified, not yet available: config validate \-\-internal.
.PP
config show prints the effective configuration. With \-\-explain, or with keys
named, it prints each key in turn, every key when none is named: its value,
source, default, environment variable, reload class, and lock; a key not in
the configuration is error: not found. A key whose value is a place karvi
writes or reads has, after its default, a resolved: line, the path the next
activity in process would use, found by the activity's own rule without
creating anything, or error: CODE: message where the activity would refuse;
a candidate present on the host and passed by follows as a passed: line with
its reason. The lines come from the configuration this invocation loads,
which its job runs under on every path; a running daemon keeps only its
socket, state, and log under the basedir it started with.
.\" END GENERATED DESCRIPTION
.SH FILES
.B config generate
with no file, or
.BR \- ,
writes the full reference configuration to standard output, every key with
its default and its comment;
.B \-\-minimal
a short starting file.
Given a file it writes it at 0600 and refuses one that exists unless
.BR \-\-force .
.B config validate
checks a file, a directory of
.I .toml
files, or, with neither, the configuration karvi would load;
.B config show
prints the effective configuration, a key's sources and lock with
.BR \-\-explain .
The files karvi reads and their order are in
.BR karvi (1)
CONFIGURATION.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR karvi (1)
